Alone in the Dark 1.0 -- Amiga port

This package runs the original Macintosh Alone in the Dark 1.0 game code.
Original game data is not included. Supply your own unmodified
AloneInTheDark.img_.sit archive when the Installer asks for it.

Installation
------------
Open Install using Amiga Installer 43 or newer. Install WHDLoad 17 or newer
first and provide a Kickstart 3.1 image with its matching .RTB in
Devs:Kickstarts or WHDCOMMON:. Supported names are kick40068.A1200,
kick40068.A4000 and kick40063.A600. These files are not included.

Allow 24 MB free in the temporary drawer and 8 MB at the destination.
Use a hard disk temporary drawer when RAM is limited. The extractor needs
about 2.7 MB of working allocations, plus its executable and the OS. It checks the exact original version, every
installed file, resource fork and Finder record. Keep the archive compressed.

Use the installed AloneInTheDark icon to launch through WHDLoad. F10 quits.
Saved games are kept when updating an installation in place. Selecting Remove
in the Installer explicitly deletes the existing drawer, including saves.

Requirements
------------
AGA, 68020 or better, 2 MB Chip RAM and 8 MB Fast RAM. A 68030 or faster is
recommended. Native 68020/68030 intro and first-floor endurance tests pass;
4 MB Fast RAM fails startup. WHDLoad startup, attic play and Save/Load pass
on a 68030 with 2 MB Chip and 8 MB Fast. More Fast RAM allows more PRELOAD
caching. WHDLoad and its Kickstart image also need memory outside the game.

The game uses a normal 4 KB Amiga process stack: measured usage is about
2.1 KB through startup, gameplay, Save/Load and exit. Private Macintosh and
music stacks are allocated internally. No Shell Stack increase is needed.

Controls
--------
Use the keyboard for movement and actions; Enter opens the action menu.
Use the original game menus for saving, loading and starting a new game.
F10 exits WHDLoad. The original Cmd-Q equivalent uses the right Amiga key
with Q. See the repository README for the complete control mapping.

Source and support
